            <h2>👋 Hey, I'm Vasilis</h2>
            <br />
            <blockquote>
                <strong>Senior Software Engineer</strong> based in Edinburgh, Scotland. I design and build backend systems, APIs, and wrangle data pipelines mostly in .NET and Azure.
            </blockquote>

            <h2>💻 What I Do</h2>
            <p>With over 10 years of experience in software engineering, I specialize in backend development designing and building scalable API-driven systems and data integration services, particularly in cloud environments like Azure.</p>
            <p>I've contributed to cloud-native transformations, led the design of robust data workflows using Azure Durable Functions, Blob Storage, and SQL, and built scalable REST APIs with .NET Core. I'm also a strong advocate for automation, clean architecture, best practices but above all...solving problems.</p>
            <p>I excel at problem-solving and spotting gaps and edge cases early. I enjoy breaking down big challenges into manageable parts, asking the right questions, and finding clean, practical solutions that balance business goals with technical soundness all while making the most out of AI to close technical skill gaps, knowledge gaps and supercharge productivity.</p>

            <h2>💼 Where I've Worked</h2>
            <p></p>
            <h3>Mews (2025 - preset)</h3>
            <p>I recently joined Mews Fintech department and working in financial services team to help our hospitality clients automate their payment processes.

            <h3>Craneware plc (2020 - 2025)</h3>
            <p>Worked as a <strong>Senior Software Engineer</strong> in the Data Innovations department, where I was responsible for making U.S. healthcare regulatory data available to Craneware products and clients.</p>
            <p>I designed, built, and maintained tools and services to ingest, validate, apply business logic to, and expose regulatory datasets via APIs. These datasets were sourced regularly from various external agencies, and I've led the design and implementation of robust ETL pipelines using Azure Durable Functions, Blob Storage triggers, and Azure SQL enabling scalable and maintainable ingestion of complex healthcare data.</p>

            <h3>Zonal Retail Data Systems (2017 - 2020)</h3>
            <p>Worked as a <strong>Software Engineer</strong> within an agile team to deliver web microservices and REST APIs as part of Zonal's transformation of its core EPOS software into a fully cloud-based platform.</p>
            <p>Focused on backend development using C# with .NET Core, following a microservices architecture and deploying through CI/CD pipelines in Azure DevOps. Leveraged Docker for containerization and Kubernetes for orchestration and deployment across environments.</p>

            <h3>Cgsoft LTD (2014 - 2017)</h3>
            <p>After some solid academic foundations and projects during my Software Engineering Master that concluded with a java-Android app backed with a LAMP stack API+admin web app and some freelance wordpress projects on the side I have joined Cgsoft LTD.</p> 
            <p>I started my career as a "jack of all trades" type of <strong>Software Engineer</strong> contributing to a variety of projects involving complex business and application logic, primarily implemented in T-SQL (stored procedures, triggers, functions) across Desktop and Web applications.</p>
            <p>Worked with a wide range of technologies, including .NET/C# (WebApi2, .NET Core) for backend services, AngularJS 1.5, MVC5, and WebForms for frontend development, and WordPress/PHP for CMS-driven sites.</p>
            <p>Key projects included developing the API layer (.NET 4.5 / WebApi2) for Piraeus Bank's Real Estate web platform, designing and building the company's website from scratch using WordPress, and creating a product order and inquiry app using AngularJS, DevExtreme, and C# WebApi2.</p>

